ElecSus — Authors
=================

ElecSus is open-source software for calculating the electric susceptibility,
refractive index and transmission spectra of thermal alkali-metal vapours, and
for fitting the model to experimental data. Authorship by version:

Versions 1-3 (2014-2018)
  M. A. Zentile
  J. Keaveney
  L. Weller
  D. Whiting
  C. S. Adams
  I. G. Hughes

Version 4 (2026)
  S. A. Wrathmall
  R. M. Potvliege

The per-file copyright headers record the authors of individual modules.
Copyright is held by the respective authors under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (see LICENSE.txt).

If ElecSus contributes to a publication, please cite:
  M. A. Zentile et al., Comput. Phys. Commun. 189, 162-174 (2015)
  J. Keaveney et al., Comput. Phys. Commun. 224, 311-324 (2018)
